Research Engine Phase 4: analysis by sentence, corrections, data advice, discoveries, data questions

The Research Engine audit's Phase 4 (automated analysis), on top of Phases
1–3. The analysis layer is reachable by sentence and explains itself from
the data. Nothing existing was removed: the plan, the runs, the verdicts
and the findings read as they did; the new things sit beside them.

Engine: tests planned by sentence ("run a t-test of X by Y", "test whether
X differs by Y", "add a chi-square of X by Y", "correlate X with Y",
"regress Y on X") through the action gate, the method named or chosen from
the variables' levels, wrong pairings refused with the right method, a
repeat a no-op; the plan queried for what reads a variable ("what analyses
are planned for X", "is X in the plan"); planned items removed by sentence;
data questions ("which groups prefer Brand A", "what share of women chose
X", "what is the average X by Y", "does X differ by Y", "are women more
satisfied than men", "which brand is most considered") read into a
DataQuery — the option, the question, the cut, the population — as a new
`query` Interpretation kind the Studio answers on the data.

Analytics: posthoc.ts (Holm / Bonferroni / Benjamini–Hochberg; pairwise
comparisons with the pairs' p adjusted as a family); dataAdvice.ts (the
method's assumptions checked on the actual data and the method the data
recommends); synthesis.ts (segment discovery beyond the plan, anomalies,
trends across waves — corrected as one family, held to an effect);
dataQuery.ts (a data question answered with the base, the interval, the
test, the pairs, each group against the rest). runPlan carries the
corrections by hypothesis family (adjusted p beside raw, a corrected
verdict beside the verdict), the pairs behind a significant ANOVA, the
advice (and runs the recommended test beside the planned one with
`adapt`), and the discoveries; briefText prints them.

Studio: POST /api/copilot/ask (analytics.read; the sandbox against the fake
provider sends its own rows); the card's "Read from the data" line with the
base, the test and the planned finding from the last run; the Findings tab
shows the correction summary, each finding's adjusted p, a corrected
verdict, the data advice with its recommendation, the discoveries, and
puts a discovery in the plan with one click through the engine; the run
brief carries the new fields; migration 0048 adds corrections / advice /
discoveries to analytics_runs, and analyticsRunStore.ts inserts with them
or, on an older database, without.

Tests: analytics 247 (phase4.test 11), engine 1748 (nlPhase4.test 4),
studio 284 (analyticsRunStore 3, copilot outline), scripts/
phase4-analysis-test.mjs (10 checks); full browser corpus 122 green with
the 10 known baseline failures only. Mutations: analytics 32/32 caught,
engine 25/25 caught, Studio 11/12 caught and one equivalent. See
docs/PHASE4-ANALYSIS-2026-10-09.md.

